cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Reporting the Accuracy of Approximate Quantum Circuit Simulation v0.2.2"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21851380
message: "If you use this tool or the certification protocols it checks in published work, please cite the protocol paper as below."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "ZKSF.org (Zero Kelvin Simulation Foundry)"
    email: info@zksf.org
    website: "https://zksf.org"
  - name: "Digital Venture Labs LLC"
repository-code: "https://github.com/official-dvl/zksf-zcc-verify"
url: "https://zksf.org"
abstract: >-
  Dependency-free checker for ZKSF certificates: ZCC-v0.1 and ZHF-v0.1 accuracy
  certificates, ZCC-Estimate-v0.1/v0.2 estimates and ZQEC-v0.1 error-correction
  certificates. Recomputes a certificate's declared error bound from the measured
  quantity the certificate reports, and requires the two to agree: sqrt(2*eps) for
  matrix product state truncation, the discarded coefficient mass for Pauli
  propagation, zero for exact and stabilizer methods, and a Hellinger fidelity
  within the unit interval for runs on quantum hardware, with the coincidence share
  recomputed for photonic runs. For a neural ground state it recomputes the energy
  ceiling and checks the floor against Weinstein's or Temple's inequality; for
  zero-noise extrapolation it checks that the estimate is marked uncertified at one
  sigma; for error correction it recomputes every logical error rate's Wilson 95%
  interval, the least-squares suppression factor and its joint 95% range. Also checks record
  structure and confirms no account data or circuit source is present. It
  establishes that a certificate is well formed and self-consistent; it does not
  establish that the underlying measurement was honestly made.
keywords:
  - quantum computing
  - quantum circuit simulation
  - error bounds
  - certification
  - verification
  - reproducibility
license: MIT
version: 0.2.2
